Summary (explanatory only; the sections below prevail)
  - Using it to teach and learn - schools, educational institutions,
    teachers, students - is free.
  - Selling it, charging for it, or using it for company work or a for-profit
    business is not allowed.
  - This is NOT an "open source" license as defined by the OSI. The source is
    public, but use is limited to educational purposes.

1. Definitions
  1. "Software" means the source code, documentation, configuration, tests and
     build tools in this repository, and copies or modifications of them,
     excluding the items listed in Section 5.
  2. "Educational Purpose" means use of the Software by a school (including
     kindergarten, primary, secondary, higher, special and alternative
     schools), a lifelong-education or teacher-training institution, or an
     education administration body, or by a teacher, instructor, student or
     other learner, in order to teach, to learn, or to run educational
     activities.
  3. "Commercial Purpose" means any of: (a) receiving payment for access to,
     use of, support for or hosting of the Software or a service built on it;
     (b) earning revenue from the use of the Software through advertising,
     sale of data or similar; (c) using it as part of a for-profit business's
     products, services or operations.

2. Grant
  The copyright holder grants everyone, for Educational Purposes only, free of
  charge and non-exclusively, the right to: (1) use the Software, including
  installing it and running it on your own server; (2) copy it; (3) modify it;
  (4) distribute it free of charge to users who use it for Educational
  Purposes, provided that you include this license text and the copyright
  notice, state that you changed it if you did, and the same terms apply to
  the recipient. Viewing and forking this repository within GitHub is governed
  by the GitHub Terms of Service and is separate from this license.

3. Restrictions
  You may not: (1) use or provide the Software for a Commercial Purpose;
  (2) use it for anything other than an Educational Purpose (for example,
  general business collaboration or a service for customers); (3) sell it,
  offer it as paid hosting or a subscription, or include it in a paid product;
  (4) remove or alter the copyright notice or this license text; (5) grant
  broader rights than this license or redistribute it under a different
  license; (6) use the copyright holder's or the repository's name to suggest
  endorsement (factual attribution is allowed).

4. Other permissions
  Any use outside Section 2, including Commercial Purposes, needs the
  copyright holder's prior written permission. Ask by opening an Issue at
  https://github.com/dhsy3206/edulet.

5. What this license does not cover
  These are not the copyright holder's, and this license grants no rights in
  them: (1) public/vendor/qrcode.js - QRCode for JavaScript by Kazuhiko Arase
  (MIT), under the terms in public/vendor/LICENSE-qrcode.txt; (2)
  seed/demo-board.json and seed/img/ - material transcribed from a public
  reference board, whose rights belong to its original rights holder; you must
  obtain permission from them separately; (3) third-party trademarks and logos
  (for example Google and the Google "G" logo, Padlet, QR Code), which are
  subject to their owners' guidelines.

6. No warranty; limitation of liability
  The Software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, including
  merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. To
  the extent permitted by law, the copyright holder is not liable for any
  damages arising from its use.

7. Termination
  If you breach this license, your permission ends immediately. It continues,
  however, if you fix every breach within 30 days after being notified of it.

8. Governing law and interpretation
  This license is governed by the laws of the Republic of Korea. If the Korean
  and English texts differ, the Korean text governs.
